            {
                "author_name": "Romain ROUYER",
                "fallback": "Romain ROUYER commented on NeuroTechX Conectome EU: \"Suite à une discussion avec Sophie (NTX London), voici une proposition faite auprès des admin NTX\n\n___\n\nProposition for a NTX EU BIR\n\nThere are several informal exchanges for the constitution of a European NTX connectome, lead by Bryan, Hans &amp; cie. BIR could be a great way to kick this off, given the growth in EU chapters this year.\n\nBy discussing with Hans on one side and Sophie on the other side, I allow myself to summarize a suggestion here for the BIR event.\n\n- common voice : calendar coordination (e.g. 1 day, 1 city) around a common theme (a ground to help highlight the value of Europe's dynamic ecosystem)\n- accessibility : allowing people to go\/follow online to as many BIRs as possible with online or hybrid event\n- chapter introduction : set aside a time for each of us (EU Chapter) to introduce ourselves quickly, with a pitch of our chapter to highlight the diversity of EU initiatives (e.g. 10-15 min tour of Europe following the introduction of the NeuroTechX network, at the beginning of each local event or during an introduction \/ online communication campaign)\n\nI suggest to create a dedicated slack channel to facilitate exchanges between all of NTX EU chapter leader interested by this initiative :rocket:\n\nThis is an opportunity to synchronise all together and start some form of collaboration to move towards a NTX EU Connectome.\"",
                "text": "Suite à une discussion avec Sophie (NTX London), voici une proposition faite auprès des admin NTX\n\n___\n\nProposition for a NTX EU BIR\n\nThere are several informal exchanges for the constitution of a European NTX connectome, lead by Bryan, Hans &amp; cie. BIR could be a great way to kick this off, given the growth in EU chapters this year.\n\nBy discussing with Hans on one side and Sophie on the other side, I allow myself to summarize a suggestion here for the BIR event.\n\n- common voice : calendar coordination (e.g. 1 day, 1 city) around a common theme (a ground to help highlight the value of Europe's dynamic ecosystem)\n- accessibility : allowing people to go\/follow online to as many BIRs as possible with online or hybrid event\n- chapter introduction : set aside a time for each of us (EU Chapter) to introduce ourselves quickly, with a pitch of our chapter to highlight the diversity of EU initiatives (e.g. 10-15 min tour of Europe following the introduction of the NeuroTechX network, at the beginning of each local event or during an introduction \/ online communication campaign)\n\nI suggest to create a dedicated slack channel to facilitate exchanges between all of NTX EU chapter leader interested by this initiative :rocket:\n\nThis is an opportunity to synchronise all together and start some form of collaboration to move towards a NTX EU Connectome.",
